cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Kwan in your work, please cite it using the details below."
type: software
title: "Kwan: an open-source learning path engine for Ghanaian primary maths"
abstract: >-
  Kwan (Twi for "path") tells a pupil which maths skill to learn next,
  explains why, and sets the practice in everyday Ghanaian life. It organises
  skills with the learning indicator codes of the NaCCA Standards-Based
  Curriculum for Mathematics, Basic 1 to Basic 6, links them in a prerequisite
  map, tracks each pupil with a multi-level Elo learner model that passes
  evidence along the map and allows for forgetting, and recommends the next
  skills with reasons a teacher can read. Kwan is not reviewed, approved or
  endorsed by NaCCA or the Ministry of Education.
authors:
  - family-names: "Ray"
    given-names: "Rofy"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rofyray/kwan"
